<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mulinuʻu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mulinuʻu is a low peninsula on the western side of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apia">Apia</a> harbour on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upolu">Upolu</a>, Samoa. Samoan chiefs set up their central government there in 1873, and it remained a seat of royal and rival Samoan governments during the conflicts of the late 19th century. It is today the site of the Samoan parliament house and of the tombs of several paramount chiefs.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mulinuu.jpg" alt="Mulinuʻu" width="320" height="239" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tattersall Studios · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mulinu%27u_by_Tattersall_Studios_-_Samoa_1893-1949.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
